From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] comgr: avoid host assertions in GNU header coexistence test

Use constexpr std::array and std::get in the device kernel to keep testing
GNU header coexistence without calling the host-only bounds assertion
handler enabled by this distribution. No matching upstream fix was found
in the file history at the time of the LLVM 24 backport review.

--- a/amd/comgr/test-lit/compile-hip-system-libstdcxx.hip
+++ b/amd/comgr/test-lit/compile-hip-system-libstdcxx.hip
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 static_assert(std::tuple_size<std::array<int, 3>>::value == 3, "array size");

 extern "C" __attribute__((global)) void test_kernel(int *out) {
-  std::array<int, 3> a = {1, 2, 3};
-  out[0] = a[0] + a[1] + a[2];
+  // Check header coexistence with compile-time checked indexing. GNU array
+  // operator[] may call a host-only assertion handler even for valid indices.
+  constexpr std::array<int, 3> a = {1, 2, 3};
+  out[0] = std::get<0>(a) + std::get<1>(a) + std::get<2>(a);
 }
